===Etymology===
From {{inh|is|non|hǫnd}}, from {{inh|is|gem-pro|*handuz}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{IPA|is|/hœnt/}}
*: {{rhymes|is|œnt|s=1}}

===Noun===
{{is-noun|@@}}

# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[hand]]
#: {{syn|is|lúka<qq:especially a large one>}}
#: {{ux|is|Mér er illt í '''hendinni'''.|My '''hand''' hurts.}}
# {{lb|is|anatomy}} [[arm]]
# [[side]], [[hand]]
#: {{syn|is|hlið}}
#: {{ux|is|Og ykkur á hægri '''hönd''' sjáið þið Esjuna.|And on your right '''hand''' you can see the Esja.}}
# [[hand]], [[handwriting]] (someone's personal style of writing)

====Usage notes====
* The dative form ''hönd'' is used in the sense of “handwriting”.
* A nominative-accusative plural form ''höndur'' existed, but is obsolete.
* The alternative form {{m|is|hendi}} is sometimes used for nominative and accusative singular in [[non-standard]] [[colloquial]] speech; especially regarding sports.

